    "negative_result": true,
    "statement": "D4 has ONE motor per bearing condition, so 'outer-race fault' and 'motor identity' are the same variable. Nothing distinguishes a bearing defect from any other difference between two physical machines -- winding tolerances, mounting, alignment, age. Vibration is measurably 1.6-2.3x higher on the faulty motor across every matched scenario pair, and that measurement cannot be attributed to the bearing. Reported as a documented negative result, never as a capability."
